# Hinged door: ONE object wearing two stacked cells (footprint 1x2x1),
# authored CLOSED, facing +x, hinge at the -z pivot corner. The open pose
# (a rigid 90-degree swing about the hinge), the per-facing rotation, and
# the lower/upper split are all derived by the engine (states door) — which
# is why every box must fit the swing envelope, x below 4.
#
# The leaf is set back from the -x face so the handle can protrude past
# both leaf faces. The upper half DRAWS a divided-lite window but collides
# as the uncut slab (the lites are cosmetic to physics and light), so the
# upper leaf here is an invisible collision+light+interaction box under
# visual-only rails, stiles and mullions.
version 1
shape door
grid 12
footprint 1 2 1
states door
box all                          1 0 0    3 12 12   # leaf, lower half
box visual+interaction           0 9 9    4 11 11   # handle (lower only)
box visual                       3 1 0    4 3 1     # hinge, lower
box collision+light+interaction  1 12 0   3 24 12   # leaf, upper half (uncut)
box visual                       1 12 0   3 14 12   # bottom rail
box visual                       1 22 0   3 24 12   # top rail
box visual                       1 14 0   3 22 2    # stile, hinge side
box visual                       1 14 10  3 22 12   # stile, latch side
box visual                       1 14 5   3 22 7    # vertical mullion
box visual                       1 17 2   3 19 10   # horizontal mullion
box visual                       3 21 0   4 23 1    # hinge, upper
